1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,990
An AI prediction is useful only when an operator knows when to trust it.

2
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:11,700
This research demo brings uncertainty, evidence, and operational context into
one decision console.

3
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:16,660
Machine learning estimates equipment health and future electricity demand.

4
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:19,640
Conformal calibration adds prediction intervals.

5
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:26,480
The system then turns interval evidence into alerts and retrieves relevant
procedures to support the operator.

6
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:32,320
In the marine replay, a public gas turbine simulator provides the operating
data.

7
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:35,450
The blue band shows uncertainty around the health estimate.

8
00:00:35,570 --> 00:00:43,230
When that band crosses the action threshold, the agent raises a watch alert:
gather evidence before committing to maintenance.

9
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:48,050
A confirmed alert requires the entire interval to pass the threshold.

10
00:00:48,170 --> 00:00:52,180
This reduces premature escalation, but can delay confirmation.

11
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:58,960
The console keeps both watch and confirmed states visible, alongside the
conventional point estimate alarms.

12
00:00:59,850 --> 00:01:03,330
Operators do not always have time for a long explanation.

13
00:01:03,450 --> 00:01:09,440
Simulated alert pressure switches the advisory from a detailed view to a
focused set of actions.

14
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:13,040
The underlying prediction and alert decision stay the same.

15
00:01:13,850 --> 00:01:17,880
The energy console forecasts Finnish residual load three hours ahead.

16
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,460
Calibrated intervals support reserve planning, and rolling coverage charts
monitor performance.

17
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:27,720
Coverage applies across cases, not to every individual forecast.

18
00:01:28,350 --> 00:01:33,150
Optional GPT O S S writes explanations from retrieved knowledge.

19
00:01:33,270 --> 00:01:36,210
Numerical confidence stays computed by the app.

20
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:42,350
Operators can inspect citations, and an offline composer takes over if the
language model fails.

21
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,030
A research demonstration, not a production safety system.

22
00:01:46,150 --> 00:01:52,360
Public data and synthetic manuals support the next step: human review and
validation with real operators.
